From 52e7a3ced87160757397c1b80a3b13d9ab15c2da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:14:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] nouveau: restore falcon RTOS message queues (needed for
 Pascal)

On GP102-GP108 secure boot runs the ACR on SEC2, which is itself an
LS-managed falcon running NVIDIA's RTOS. FECS and GPCCS are started by
posting ACR_CMD_BOOTSTRAP_FALCON to that RTOS through the falcon
message queue, on every GR init and not only on reset.

The message queue was stubbed with NOT_IMPLEMENTED_STOP, so a Pascal
card hung forever in nvkm_msgqueue_ctor() as soon as the SEC2 firmware
was loaded. cmd_write() also skipped cmd_queue_open(), which takes the
queue lock and computes the write position, so commands would have been
written at a stale offset with an unlocked semaphore released.

With completions available in drm-compat, msgqueue.h,
msgqueue_0148cdec.c (SEC2) and msgqueue_0137c63d.c (PMU) are back to
the upstream 5.4.302 sources. msgqueue.c keeps one AROS change: the
queue-full retry loop polls with udelay() instead of jiffies.

patches/drm-aros.diff is refreshed for these files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LaFFmUWBSJL732ja1ybwuh
